.TH TRAIL-SOURCE 5 2026-10-17 "Peios trail 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
trail-source \- Trail source tree names and layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
<root>/
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trail derives the whole site from the tree, so every name in it is meaningful
and every unrecognised name is a build error. This page is the exhaustive
grammar. Anatomy of a site is the
same material as a walkthrough.
.PP
.SS "The name shapes"
.PP
.TP
\fB<slug>.product\fR
Example: \fBpekit.product\fR; What: A product. Site root only; no order
prefix.
.TP
\fB<order>--<slug>.antho\fR
Example: \fB1--security.antho\fR; What: An anthology.
.TP
\fB<order>--<slug>.topic\fR
Example: \fB4--reference.topic\fR; What: A topic.
.TP
\fB<order>--<slug>.book\fR
Example: \fB2--pgss.book\fR; What: A book.
.TP
\fB<order>--<slug>.shelf\fR
Example: \fB3--tooling.shelf\fR; What: A shelf.
.TP
\fB<order>--<slug>\fR
Example: \fB300--tokens\fR; What: A topic subfolder or a book chapter. No
suffix.
.TP
\fB<order>--<slug>.md\fR
Example: \fB100--sids.md\fR; What: An article.
.TP
\fB<order>--<slug>.link\fR
Example: \fB3--faq.link\fR; What: A link alias.
.TP
\fB<slug>.<ext>\fR
Example: \fBlogon-flow.svg\fR; What: A co-located image. No order prefix.
.TP
\fBtrail.toml\fR
What: Configuration, at every level.
.PP
.SS "<order>"
.PP
A non-negative integer, parsed as written. \fB1\fR, \fB100\fR, and \fB007\fR
are all valid
and all mean their numeric value.
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
It is a \fBsort key only\fR  -  never shown, never part of a URL  -  **except
  inside a book**, where it _is_ the
  published section number.
.IP \(bu 2
Gaps are fine and normal.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTwo siblings sharing an order is an error\fR, since their relative order
  would then depend on nothing visible.
.IP \(bu 2
Anything not parseable as an integer is an error: no \fB1.5\fR, no \fB-1\fR,
no
  \fBfirst\fR.
.PP
.SS "a<N> — appendix orders"
.PP
\fBInside a book only.\fR An order written \fBa1\fR, \fBa2\fR, ... marks an
appendix
entry, which is lettered rather than numbered and sorts after every numbered
sibling at its level.
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
Letters are bijective base 26: \fBa1\fR → A, \fBa26\fR → Z, \fBa27\fR → AA.
.IP \(bu 2
The letter comes from the number, not from position, so gaps show through
  here too.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBa0\fR is an error: appendix orders start at \fBa1\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Outside a book, an \fBa<N>--\fR prefix is a non-numeric order prefix, and
  therefore an error.
.PP
.SS "<slug>"
.PP
Lowercase kebab-case:
.PP
.PP
.nf
ASCII lowercase letters, digits and hyphens
not empty
not starting or ending with a hyphen
.fi
.PP
\fBgetting-started\fR, \fBpgss\fR, \fBrfc-2119\fR are fine.
\fBGetting_Started\fR, \fB-draft\fR,
\fBtokens/\fR, \fBcafé\fR are not.
.PP
The slug is the URL segment, and it is what you write in a
\fB~link\fR.
.PP
.SS "<kind>"
.PP
Exactly one of \fBantho\fR, \fBtopic\fR, \fBbook\fR, \fBshelf\fR. Any other
suffix is an
error, as is a grouping directory with no suffix at all in a place where one
is expected.
.PP
.SS "What each directory can contain"
.PP
Anything not listed is a build error. Entries whose name starts with \fB.\fR
are
skipped everywhere, so \fB.git\fR, \fB.DS_Store\fR and editor droppings are
invisible
to trail.
.PP
.TP
\fBSite root\fR
Subdirectories: \fB*.product\fR, the output dir; Files: \fBtrail.toml\fR;
whatever \fBfavicon\fR, \fBcustom_css\fR, \fBhead_html\fR, \fBpassthrough\fR,
and \fB[[merge]]\fR name
.TP
\fBProduct\fR
Subdirectories: \fB.antho\fR, \fB.topic\fR, \fB.book\fR, \fB.shelf\fR; Files:
\fBtrail.toml\fR
.TP
\fBAnthology\fR
Subdirectories: \fB.antho\fR, \fB.topic\fR, \fB.book\fR, \fB.shelf\fR; Files:
\fBtrail.toml\fR
.TP
\fBShelf\fR
Subdirectories: \fB.antho\fR, \fB.topic\fR, \fB.book\fR  -  never another
\fB.shelf\fR; Files: \fBtrail.toml\fR
.TP
\fBTopic\fR
Subdirectories: \fB<order>--<slug>\fR subfolders; Files: \fBtrail.toml\fR,
\fB.md\fR, \fB.link\fR, images
.TP
\fBTopic subfolder\fR
Subdirectories: _(none  -  one level only)_; Files: \fBtrail.toml\fR,
\fB.md\fR, \fB.link\fR, images
.TP
\fBBook\fR
Subdirectories: \fB<order>--<slug>\fR chapters; Files: \fBtrail.toml\fR,
\fB.md\fR, \fB.link\fR, images
.TP
\fBBook chapter\fR
Subdirectories: \fB<order>--<slug>\fR chapters, to any depth; Files:
\fBtrail.toml\fR, \fB.md\fR, \fB.link\fR, images
.PP
The dividing line: **directories that hold groupings hold no files but
\fBtrail.toml\fR; directories that hold articles hold no grouping
directories.**
.PP
.SS "trail.toml by level"
.PP
.TP
Site root
Required?: \fBrequired\fR; Keys: see the \fBtrail.toml\fR reference
.TP
Product
Required?: \fBrequired\fR; Keys: \fBtitle\fR, \fBmonogram\fR, \fBcolor\fR,
\fBdescription\fR, \fBinline_ref\fR
.TP
Anthology
Required?: \fBrequired\fR; Keys: \fBtitle\fR, \fBdescription\fR,
\fBinline_ref\fR
.TP
Book
Required?: \fBrequired\fR; Keys: \fBtitle\fR, \fBdescription\fR, \fBshort\fR,
\fBinline_ref\fR
.TP
Topic
Required?: optional; Keys: \fBtitle\fR, \fBinline_ref\fR
.TP
Topic subfolder
Required?: optional; Keys: \fBtitle\fR, \fBinline_ref\fR
.TP
Book chapter
Required?: optional; Keys: \fBtitle\fR, \fBinline_ref\fR
.TP
Shelf
Required?: optional; Keys: \fBtitle\fR only  -  \fB\fBinline_ref\fR is an
error\fR
.PP
Unknown keys are errors at every level. Where \fBtitle\fR is optional and
absent,
it is derived from the slug: hyphens to spaces, in title case
(\fBthe-two-gates\fR
→ "The Two Gates", \fBdeveloping-for-peios\fR → "Developing for Peios").
Derived titles has the casing
rule.
.PP
.SS "Reserved names"
.PP
.TP
\fBprint\fR
Where: article slugs; Why: every container publishes a \fB/print\fR page
.TP
\fBassets\fR
Where: product slugs; Why: collides with \fB/assets\fR in the output
.TP
\fBpagefind\fR
Where: product slugs; Why: collides with \fB/pagefind\fR in the output
.PP
.SS "Images"
.PP
A co-located image is \fB<slug>.<ext>\fR where the stem is a valid slug and
the
extension is \fBlowercase\fR and one of:
.PP
.PP
.nf
png   jpg   jpeg   gif   svg   webp   avif
.fi
.PP
Anything else in an article directory falls through to the "unexpected file"
error.
.PP
.SS "Sorting"
.PP
Siblings sort by order, ascending. Inside a book, appendix entries sort after
every numbered entry at the same level, whatever their numbers.
.PP
Products are the exception: no order prefix, so they sort by the root config's
\fBfeatured\fR list first (in that list's order), then the rest by title.
.PP
.SS "Duplicates"
.PP
Within one container, both order and slug must be unique:
.PP
.PP
.nf
items 'concepts' and 'guides' share order 1
duplicate article slug 'overview'
.fi
.PP
The noun is \fBitem\fR for a container's mixed children (topics, books,
anthologies, shelves), and \fBarticle\fR inside a topic subfolder or where
only
articles can sit. Slugs are reported without their order prefixes.
.PP
Shelf contents are checked \fBflattened into their parent\fR, because a shelf
adds no URL segment  -  two shelves in one product cannot both hold a
\fBgetting-started\fR topic, since both would want the same URL.
.PP
.SS "URLs"
.PP
A page's URL is the product slug, then the slug of every container between it
and the page, with two exceptions: shelves contribute nothing, and order
prefixes contribute nothing.
.PP
.PP
.nf
peios.product/1--security.antho/2--tokens.topic/300--issuing/100--flow.md
  →  /peios/security/tokens/issuing/flow
.fi
.PP
Pages are written to disk as \fB<path>/index.html\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trail (1),
.BR trail.toml (5)
.PP
Trail Learn: https://learn.peios.org/trail/
